            "ImageUrl": "https://www.digikey.ie//mm.digikey.com/Volume0/opasdata/d220001/derivates/3/030/156/264%7E11-10C4%7E%7E8_tmb.jpg",
            "SeoDescription": "Linear circuits and component parameters remain unchanged in regard to voltage and current levels. Included in this category are amplifiers, OP Amps, video amps and modules, analog multipliers, dividers, comparators, video processing, and more.",
            "ChildCategories": [
              {
                "CategoryId": 692,
                "ParentId": 2018,
                "Name": "Comparators",
                "ProductCount": 0,
                "NewProductCount": 0,
                "ImageUrl": "https://www.digikey.ie//mm.digikey.com/Volume0/opasdata/d220001/derivates/3/100/958/564/296_14-DIP_tmb.jpg",
                "SeoDescription": "Linear comparator products are used to evaluate the relative magnitude of two analog input signals and generate a binary (two-state) output indicating which of the two is larger. Closely related to operational amplifiers in their function, linear comparators are specifically designed to tolerate the open-loop operation and large differential input conditions commonly encountered in analog comparison applications, which can cause standard operational amplifiers to behave in undesirable ways.",
                "ChildCategories": []
              }
